1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,388
My daughter is subscribed to a hundred and forty-eight YouTube channels. I had seen about ten of them. Her brother follows nineteen.

2
00:00:07,388 --> 00:00:14,853
No parent can check a hundred and forty-eight channels, so nobody does. Parental controls decide what a child may see, and then do nothing.

3
00:00:14,853 --> 00:00:17,484
HeyGilli is the agent that does that job for you.

4
00:00:18,484 --> 00:00:23,437
A parent answers a few questions about what is fine in their house, and picks what the child likes.

5
00:00:23,437 --> 00:00:24,988
That is all the setup there is.

6
00:00:25,988 --> 00:00:31,352
Then the Curator agent reads each new upload from the family's channels, against those answers.

7
00:00:31,352 --> 00:00:35,926
Clear cases it decides alone, and it shows its reasons as tags a parent can skim.

8
00:00:35,926 --> 00:00:37,676
Anything it kept back says why.

9
00:00:38,676 --> 00:00:42,332
Borderline videos wait for the parent, with the reason in two sentences.

10
00:00:42,332 --> 00:00:48,324
That is the whole relationship. The agent does the work. The parent answers only the questions that are really theirs.

11
00:00:49,324 --> 00:00:54,267
Everything Gilli kept back sits in one place, each with the sentence it wrote for keeping it.

12
00:00:54,267 --> 00:00:57,988
The parent can overrule any of them. The agent is never the last word.

13
00:00:58,988 --> 00:01:00,719
Only these channels reach Rayan.

14
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:07,916
Gilli read each one before anything from it was offered, and it never removes a channel on its own: that stays the parent's decision.

15
00:01:08,916 --> 00:01:14,772
Found a video yourself? Paste the link, and Gilli reads it against your answers before your child ever sees it.

16
00:01:15,772 --> 00:01:19,857
A parent who wants to know more about a video can just ask, in their own words.

17
00:01:19,857 --> 00:01:25,132
The Explainer agent answers from what it actually read, and says so when the answer is only the title.

18
00:01:26,132 --> 00:01:29,362
A family already on YouTube does not start from an empty shelf.

19
00:01:29,362 --> 00:01:35,156
Bring your own subscriptions in, and every channel is read against your answers before a single video is offered.

20
00:01:36,156 --> 00:01:40,422
The child's shelf looks like YouTube Kids, with only what the parent allowed.

21
00:01:40,422 --> 00:01:45,852
They can search, by typing or by voice, but only among those videos. Search never reaches YouTube.

22
00:01:46,852 --> 00:01:50,478
A child who cannot spell yet holds the microphone and says it instead.

23
00:01:50,478 --> 00:01:55,348
The words never leave the device, and the search still only reaches videos the parent allowed.

24
00:01:56,348 --> 00:02:01,162
At a natural break the video pauses, and Gilli asks about what just happened, out loud.

25
00:02:01,162 --> 00:02:08,355
The Planner agent wrote it from this video's own words, for this child's age: two or three questions a video, sized to its length.

26
00:02:08,355 --> 00:02:13,556
The child answers by talking or by tapping, the Buddy agent replies, and the video carries on.

27
00:02:14,556 --> 00:02:17,064
A child who goes quiet is not left in silence.

28
00:02:17,064 --> 00:02:23,934
After a few seconds Gilli gives a hint: a nudge back to the moment in the video, never the answer, and the clock starts again.

29
00:02:23,934 --> 00:02:26,388
They can also ask to hear the question again.

30
00:02:27,388 --> 00:02:35,270
For a child who reads, the answers can be written cards taken from the video: one right, and two a child who half-watched might believe.

31
00:02:35,270 --> 00:02:37,588
A younger child only ever gets pictures.

32
00:02:38,588 --> 00:02:45,307
A younger child gets big pictures, and questions that need no reading: one word, a tap, or a yes or no.

33
00:02:45,307 --> 00:02:51,308
A right answer gets a cheer. A wrong one gets curiosity. Nobody is ever told they are wrong.

34
00:02:52,308 --> 00:02:55,246
A parent can add a question of their own to any video.

35
00:02:55,246 --> 00:03:00,468
Gilli asks it in their words, where it fits in the video. No model rewrites a parent's question.

36
00:03:01,468 --> 00:03:07,962
Between videos there are six short games: find Gilli, catch him, letters, numbers, who am I, and spot the animal.

37
00:03:07,962 --> 00:03:15,892
The questions are written on the device for the child's age. The Playmate agent sets how hard the next round is, and nobody loses a round.

38
00:03:16,892 --> 00:03:21,015
The parent sets the day's minutes, where the breaks fall, and when the day ends.

39
00:03:21,015 --> 00:03:26,324
None of that is the model's to decide. The limits are the parent's, and the code is what enforces them.

40
00:03:27,324 --> 00:03:31,655
When the day's minutes run out, Gilli stops the video and says the parent's own line.

41
00:03:31,655 --> 00:03:36,036
Getting back out of kid mode needs the parent's PIN, so the child cannot simply leave.

42
00:03:37,036 --> 00:03:42,676
Progress is the longer view: the minutes, whether the questions are being answered, and what is worth another look.

43
00:03:43,676 --> 00:03:47,899
Each night the Digest agent reads the day and writes a short note for the parent:

44
00:03:47,899 --> 00:03:51,548
what was said, what was only heard, and one question to ask at dinner.

45
00:03:52,548 --> 00:03:55,426
Every agent's model is one line of configuration.

46
00:03:55,426 --> 00:04:03,180
Today that is Amazon Nova Pro on Amazon Bedrock, the one our eval picked. Change the line, and the same agents run on another model.

47
00:04:04,180 --> 00:04:11,894
Eight Strands agents sit behind one gateway: Curator, Planner, Buddy, Digest, Reviewer, Coach, Explainer and Playmate.

48
00:04:11,894 --> 00:04:19,804
The agents decide. The code fetches and enforces, because the guarantees a parent trusts belong in code, not in a prompt.

49
00:04:20,804 --> 00:04:23,857
Each agent gets its own tools and its own output type.

50
00:04:23,857 --> 00:04:31,772
A tool is a plain Python function, the answer comes back as a validated Pydantic object rather than text, and every call is one traced span.

51
00:04:32,772 --> 00:04:37,147
Ads still play, and creators still get paid.

52
00:04:37,147 --> 00:04:43,908
Nothing a child says is stored. Only a score and a short paraphrase.

53
00:04:44,908 --> 00:04:50,284
HeyGilli. Try it at heygilli dot com. The code and a three-part write-up are in the description.
